WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
Your friend is revising
for a test, headphones on,

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.720
music turned up.

3
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.290
"Music helps you revise," she says.

4
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.140
"I remember loads more."

5
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.610
She sounds sure.

6
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.440
But feeling sure isn't evidence.

7
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.960
Maybe the music helps.

8
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.090
Maybe it makes no difference at all.

9
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:21.050
So how could a psychologist actually
find out whether she's right?

10
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.520
In this mission, you'll turn a
claim like this into a precise,

11
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.750
testable prediction: a hypothesis.

12
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.130
You'll find out what a researcher changes,

13
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.920
the independent variable,
and what they measure,

14
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.570
the dependent variable.

15
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.160
And you'll see why anything else that could
affect the result has to be controlled.

16
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:44.040
Your mission: work out how you could test
whether music really helps you revise.
